      },
      {
        "id": 32,
        "code": "## Patrón 4: Recursión mutua\n\nLa recursión mutua ocurre cuando dos o más predicados se llaman entre sí en un ciclo.\n\n### Ejemplo: Par e impar",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 33,
        "code": "% Definir is_even e is_odd con recursión mutua\n:- dynamic is_even/1.\n:- dynamic is_odd/1.\n\n% Caso base de is_even\nis_even(0).\n\n% Recursivo de is_even: N es par si N-1 es impar\nis_even(N) :-\n    N > 0,\n    N1 is N - 1,\n    is_odd(N1).  % ← Llama a is_odd\n\n% Caso base de is_odd\nis_odd(1).\n\n% Recursivo de is_odd: N es impar si N-1 es par\nis_odd(N) :-\n    N > 1,\n    N1 is N - 1,\n    is_even(N1).  % ← Llama a is_even",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 34,
        "code": "### Probar en Prolog",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 35,
        "code": "% Probar par/impar\nis_even(0), writeln('✓ 0 is even').\nis_even(4), writeln('✓ 4 is even').\nis_odd(3), writeln('✓ 3 is odd').\nis_odd(7), writeln('✓ 7 is odd').",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "✓ 0 is even\n✓ 4 is even\n✓ 3 is odd\n✓ 7 is odd",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">✓ 0 is even\n✓ 4 is even\n✓ 3 is odd\n✓ 7 is odd</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 36,
        "code": "### Comprobar la recursión mutua",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 37,
        "code": "% Construir grafo de llamadas y encontrar SCCs\n\\+ \\+ (\n    use_module(unifyweaver(core/advanced/call_graph)),\n    use_module(unifyweaver(core/advanced/scc_detection)),\n\n    build_call_graph([is_even/1, is_odd/1], _Graph),\n    format('Call graph: ~w~n', [_Graph]),\n\n    find_sccs(_Graph, _SCCs),\n    format('SCCs (mutual recursion groups): ~w~n', [_SCCs])\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "source_sink `unifyweaver(core/advanced/call_graph)' does not exist",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"error-result\" dir=\"ltr\">source_sink `unifyweaver(core/advanced/call_graph)' does not exist</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 38,
        "code": "### Compilar a Bash",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 39,
        "code": "% Compilar el grupo de recursión mutua\n\\+ \\+ (\n    use_module(unifyweaver(core/advanced/mutual_recursion)),\n\n    compile_mutual_recursion([is_even/1, is_odd/1], [], _BashCode),\n    split_string(_BashCode, \"\\n\", \"\\r\", _BashLines),\n    append(_LibraryLines, [\"# Main dispatch: route command line calls to functions\"|_], _BashLines),\n    atomics_to_string(_LibraryLines, \"\\n\", _LibraryCode),\n    setup_call_cleanup(\n        open('../output/even_odd_demo.sh', write, _Stream),\n        write(_Stream, _LibraryCode),\n        close(_Stream)),\n    writeln('✓ Compiled is_even/is_odd to Bash with shared memoization')\n).",
        "type": "code",
        "language": "prolog",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "true.",
        "lastOutputHtml": "<pre class=\"text-result\" dir=\"ltr\">true.</pre>"
      },
      {
        "id": 40,
        "code": "### Probar el Bash generado",
        "type": "markdown",
        "language": "markdown",
        "name": "",
        "lastOutput": "",
        "lastOutputHtml": ""
      },
      {
        "id": 41,
        "code": "source ../output/even_odd_demo.sh\necho \"Probando is_even e is_odd:\"\nis_even 0 >/dev/null && echo \"✓ 0 es par\"\nis_even 4 >/dev/null && echo \"✓ 4 es par\"\nis_odd 3 >/dev/null && echo \"✓ 3 es impar\"\nis_odd 7 >/dev/null && echo \"✓ 7 es impar\"\nis_even 5 >/dev/null 2>&1 || echo \"✓ 5 no es par\"",
